\f1\fs22 The threes Sages returned to the laboratory with Chip reluctantly in tow. Sarah had insisted that the former Fridge Force agent attend this "important consultation" despite his protests. They found The Johnny standing before a significantly altered testing apparatus, dark circles under his eyes suggesting he\'92d barely slept since their last meeting.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91The temporal matrix calibration was a stroke of genius,\'92 The Johnny admitted. Shilo tittered but The Johnny was too excited by their progress to maintain his usual veneer of superiority. \'91Look at what we've uncovered.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The holographic display now showed not just the oscillating patterns that had haunted Sarah\'92s dreams, but what appeared to be script\'97hundreds of lines of strange symbols flowing in columns that rotated slowly in three-dimensional space.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91We still can't read it,\'92 The Johnny continued, \'91but we've confirmed it's definitely language\'97or rather, languages. Multiple writing systems, possibly from different civilisations, possibly across the multiverse.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91If there 
\f2\i is
\f1\i0  such a thing as a multiverse, young Johnny.\'92 Kleo tilted his head quizzically. \'91We are yet to prove that.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chilo circled the display with practiced nonchalance. \'91The next step would be to activate the translations,\'92 he said as if uttered a random thought.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Johnny frowned, then tried to cover for his inability to understand a single thing the Sages said.  \'91Yes, of course. It\'92s on the roadmap. Right now, I\'92m isolating a referential baseline to deriving translation algorithms.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The others hid their smirk behind hands and florid sleeve cuffs. They all knew The Johnny was taking credit for something one of the team\'97usually the most lowly paid\'97was achieving.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chilo nodded sympathetically. \'91Though in my studies of ancient transmission systems, I've found that sometimes the key is hidden in the medium itself.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleo coughed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chip added, \'91But then, the risks\'97\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91What risks?\'92 The Johnny's tone sharpened. What key?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Earthquakes, continental lighting storms, seas boiling,\'92 Chip warned.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91What, so just the usual apocalyptic promises?\'92 The Johnny challenged. \'91I\'92ve personally been working on all the safeguards,\'92 he added, which roughly translated to, 
\f2\i A junior team somewhere whose names I don\'92t recall are working on it.
\f1\i0 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chip was about to object, but sublimated his fears into a heaving sigh from his bear-sized chest. No one was listening to him anyway. He resolved rather playing the role of the constant doom-sayer and thereby having his every thought dismissed , he need to time his run, wait for the evidence to mount. He imagined the meeting where he\'92s triumphantly announced, 
\f2\i I really thought this could work, but
\f1\i0  \'85 and then lay out the incontrovertible proof. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91We, the Seven Sages\'97\'92 Kleo began.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91All three of you,\'92 Chip interjected.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleo nodded graciously, as if he had all the time in the world, which he probably believed. \'91Ancient writings suggest that energies of the kind emitted by Gyges Discs in certain configurations may do more than just channel messages\'97they may be designed to transmit them.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Can we read these ancient writings?\'92 Chip folded his arms arms across chest, then immediately regretted being drawn into a confrontation.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleo shrugged enigmatically. \'91Like most arcana, young Mr Stockwell, they require certain esoteric perspectives to interpret.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chip grunted and held his powder dry.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91So you\'92re suggesting we could use the discs to communicate with other universes?\'92 The Johnny asked, then instantly froze with fear. One should never ask questions in business meetings; it made you look stupid.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Theoretically,\'92 Shilo replied.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Good, because I\'92d already thought of that,\'92 The Johnny said.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91You have?\'92 Chilo asked and smiled in such a way that The Johnny thought he was either delighted or was about to eat him raw.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Ah, yes,\'92 The Johnny stalled while his mind raced, by which we mean it ran at a cognitive load only slightly greater than doing a junior crossword. \'91But we need to experiment with other configurations,\'92 he improvised. \'91We need more\'85 Gyges Discs.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chip almost choked.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91That\'92s brilliant insight,\'92 Chilo observed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Yes, it is rather, isn\'92t it?\'92 The Johnny blathered and exhaled in relief. Yet again, his genius had pulled a multi-dimensional rabbit out his singularly dimensioned butt. But it was obvious wasn\'92t it? If two Gyges Discs were better than one, then any number of Gyges Discs would be better than, say, two.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Johnny nodded slowly, less from confidence than a forlorn desire to entrain his brain to keep producing the kind of brilliance it had just gifted him with. He calculated on his fingers how such a breakthrough would transform his reputation. \'91Dr. Quark has been reluctant to increase power to the discs after what happened in initial testing, but it\'92s all just a matter of configuration and stability.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Dr. Quark is prudent,\'92 Chilo conceded. \'91And yet, prudence produces nothing new. No new insight, no new connections.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91No new glory,\'92 Shilo added for The Johnny\'92s benefit. While he and the other sages had their disagreements, they all knew The Johnny was the perfect chump for enabling their mostly consistent agenda. He moved closer to the control panel, pointing to settings without actually touching them. \'91With threes Gyges Discs,\'92 he said in the tone of a Monty Python fan reciting \'93The Spanish Inquisition\'94 sketch, \'91the harmonic resonance between your phase variance compensator and the discs in the right  configuration might stabilise a feedback loop that would amplify the signal without requiring dangerous external power inputs.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91That's exactly what caused the Rotherhithe Stasis Collapse!\'92 Chip exclaimed, then immediately looked horrified at what he'd revealed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Come now, Chip,\'92 The Johnny was basting in his own smugness. \'91We\'92re talking about components found in every stasis unit in the land. Aren\'92t you being over-dramatic?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chip gulped and silently cursed. This is what he was afraid of: being dismissed as a broken record of a proper of doom. \'91It violates at least seventeen sections of the Refrigeration Secrets Act," he said weakly.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Ah, so your objections are administrative, based on politics rather than physics,\'92 The Johnny asserted triumphantly. \'91Very well then, Mr Stockwell. How about four discs?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Or five,\'92 Chilo encouraged, delighted at the direction the meeting was taking.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Oh, Jesus mother-taxing Mary,\'92 Chip cursed and made for the door. \'91I need to talk with Ms Jacobson.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91She won\'92t help you, you know,\'92 The Johnny called after him. \'91You need to understand whose pockets your superiors are in.\'92 Again with the smug smile. \'91Sarah and I have been the best of intimates for years!\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>An awkward pause soured the air.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Very good then.\'92 Chilo anticipated closing the meeting on a high note. \'91We are in agreement? A configuration of five Gyges Discs?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Shilo nodded as if weighing the proposal.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kelo looked at the floor solemnly. \'91It is as the prophecy predicted: 
\f2\i And the power of the light shall be bestowed upon the keepers of time and space in the likeness of a pentagram
\f1\i0 .\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Such a profound moment of stillness and silence fell upon the room, that even Kleo\'92s tinnitus gave him a short reprieve.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91The keepers of time and space\'92, The Johnny repeated while nodding. He straightened as if he was an Olympic athlete receiving their first gold medal. \'91I like the sound of that. I think I might put it on my voicemail greeting.\'92
